    "updated_at": "2024-10-03T16:47:27Z",
    "body": "> background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\r\n\r\nI do agree that it seems like we should adjust the default background color to account for dark/light mode. I'm not a UX person, so I can't comment on the right **way** to do that, but I'm supportive of trying to change it. There's a chance that it's not web compatible to change the backdrop color at this point, but it might be? Presuming this is a real problem on dark-mode-supporting sites, I would assume they've already overridden the backdrop color, so it won't break things to change the default. But who knows.",
